The $B_s^0ightarrow D_s^{*-}\mu^{+}
u_{\mu}$ decay rate has been analyzed in the context of QCD sum rules to investigate its differential behavior with respect to the squared mass of the muon-neutrino pair. By utilizing a complete set of local and power corrections for vector and axial currents, we have obtained a comprehensive expression for the differential decay rate. We have then used this expression to explain previously observed differential decay rates in $B_s^0ightarrow D_s^{*-}\mu^{+}
u_{\mu}$ and $Bightarrow D^{*-}\mu^{+}
u_{\mu}$ modes. Furthermore, we have provided differential predictions for the $B_s^0ightarrow D_s^{*-}\mu^{+}
u_{\mu}$ decay rate.
